Spec: Flexible DB Where In Feature

Purpose:
  Replace hardcoded or single-field JSON arguments (like 'companycode') with a flexible 'db_where_in' JSON structure for dynamic SELECT query generation in Oracle and PostgreSQL collectors.

Platform: Go/Linux

References:
  ../../../collector-layer/collector-layer.sdd

Can modify:
  ../../../collector-layer/mitm_collector_employee-de_ora/main.go
  ../../../collector-layer/mitm_collector_employee_ora/main.go
  ../../../collector-layer/mitm_collector_ora/main.go
  ../../../collector-layer/mitm_collector_pg/main.go

Must:
  The CollectorArgs structure must parse `db_where_in` as a key-value mapping where keys are column names and values are arrays of strings.
  Column names specified in `db_where_in` must be strictly validated against the `identifierRegex` to prevent SQL injection.
  The values must be passed as parameterized query arguments (bind variables) to the database driver.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Update mitm_collector_employee_ora to use `db_where_in` instead of `companycode`.
  [x] #2 Update mitm_collector_employee-de_ora to use `db_where_in` dynamically instead of hardcoded `AND e.companycode IN ('A1', 'DE')`.
  [x] #3 Add `db_where_in` support to mitm_collector_ora.
  [x] #4 Add `db_where_in` support to mitm_collector_pg.
